  "explanation": "The Poisson problem -nabla^2 u = f with zero Dirichlet boundary conditions has an exact, strictly linear solution operator u = A^{-1} f (discrete Green's function). Because the source family consists of smooth functions (Gaussians and low-frequency sine modes), their spatial correlations produce an extremely rapid singular-value decay (99.9% energy in << 100 modes). Consequently, ridge regression with N=100-1000 samples spans the active subspace completely and directly inverts the discrete differential operator with near-machine precision."
